module
-- upstream: candidate

public import Complexity.Crypto.Computational.Homomorphic.FixedKey.Correctness
public import Complexity.Crypto.Computational.Homomorphic.FixedKey.Security
public import Complexity.Crypto.Computational.Homomorphic.FixedKey.PolyTime

/-!
# Fully homomorphic encryption from a circular-secure bootstrappable scheme

One sampled base key and its self-encrypted secret define a fixed-key scheme permitting every
finite Boolean circuit, without a depth parameter in key generation. The actual algorithms have
perfect correctness, unchanged polynomial secret and ciphertext widths, polynomial decryption
circuits, uniform native efficiency and IND-CPA security. `FixedKey.evaluate_spec` additionally
allows prior evaluation outputs as inputs and preserves their width and plaintext under that
same key.

The input assumptions concern the base scheme and its actual decryption circuits. In particular,
`Encryption.CircularSecure` is the explicit joint one-key real-versus-zero experiment, in addition
to ordinary base IND-CPA. This is a conditional bootstrapping construction, not an instantiation
of the premises by a concrete lattice scheme. No circuit privacy or exact concrete-security
loss is asserted.

## Main results

* `Cslib.Crypto.Homomorphic.FixedKey.fullyHomomorphic`: correctness for all finite circuits,
  compactness, native efficiency and security of the same constructed algorithms.

## References

* [C. Gentry, *Fully homomorphic encryption using ideal lattices*, Section 2, the self-loop
  construction][Gentry2009]
* [D. Boneh, S. Halevi, M. Hamburg and R. Ostrovsky, *Circular-Secure Encryption from Decision
  Diffie-Hellman*, Section 2.1][BonehHaleviHamburgOstrovsky2008]
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Cslib.Crypto.Homomorphic.FixedKey

open Circuits Probability Turing.MultiTapeTM

/-- A circular-secure bootstrappable base scheme yields one compact, efficient, IND-CPA scheme
for all finite Boolean circuits. All conclusions refer to `scheme D`; its key generator takes
only the security parameter, and its decryption circuits are exactly those generated by `D`.
The stronger `evaluate_spec` also certifies arbitrary repeated evaluation. -/
theorem fullyHomomorphic {E : Scheme} {secretWidth ciphertextWidth : ℕ → ℕ}
    (D : DecryptionCircuits E secretWidth ciphertextWidth)
    (hE : E.Correct) (hwidth : E.FixedWidth secretWidth ciphertextWidth)
    (hboot : Scheme.Bootstrappable D)
    (hsecure : Encryption.INDCPA E.keyGen E.encrypt)
    (hcircular : Encryption.CircularSecure E.keyGen E.encrypt)
    (hkeyGen : IsPPTOn encUnary (encPair encBits encBits) E.keyGen)
    (hencrypt : IsPPTOn (encPair encUnary (encPair encBits encBool)) encBits
      (fun p => E.encrypt p.1 p.2.1 p.2.2))
    (hevaluate : IsPPTOn
      (encPair encUnary (encPair encBits (encPair (Boolean.encCircuit 1) (encList encBits))))
      encBits (fun p => E.evaluate p.1 p.2.1 p.2.2.1 p.2.2.2))
    (hD : ComputableInPolyTime
      (fun n => (⟨_, D.circuit n⟩ : Σ m, Circuit Boolean.signature m 1))
      encUnary (Boolean.encCircuit 1)) :
    let F := scheme D
    F.Correct ∧
      (∀ n c, F.permitted n c) ∧
      F.FixedWidth secretWidth ciphertextWidth ∧
      PolynomiallyBounded secretWidth ∧ PolynomiallyBounded ciphertextWidth ∧
      PolynomiallyBounded (fun n => ((decryptionCircuits D).circuit n).size) ∧
      IsPPTOn encUnary (encPair encBits encBits) F.keyGen ∧
      IsPPTOn (encPair encUnary (encPair encBits encBool)) encBits
        (fun p => F.encrypt p.1 p.2.1 p.2.2) ∧
      ComputableInPolyTime
        (fun p : ℕ × List Bool × List Bool => F.decrypt p.1 p.2.1 p.2.2)
        (encPair encUnary (encPair encBits encBits)) encBool ∧
      IsPPTOn
        (encPair encUnary (encPair encBits (encPair (Boolean.encCircuit 1) (encList encBits))))
        encBits (fun p => F.evaluate p.1 p.2.1 p.2.2.1 p.2.2.2) ∧
      Encryption.INDCPA F.keyGen F.encrypt :=
  ⟨correct D hE hwidth hboot, fun _ _ => trivial, fixedWidth D hE hwidth hboot,
    (polynomiallyBounded_widths D hD).1, (polynomiallyBounded_widths D hD).2,
    polynomiallyBounded_decryptionSize D hD, isPPTOn_scheme_keyGen hkeyGen hencrypt D,
    isPPTOn_scheme_encrypt hencrypt D, computableInPolyTime_scheme_decrypt D hD,
    isPPTOn_scheme_evaluate hencrypt D hD hevaluate,
    indCPA_scheme D hsecure hcircular hkeyGen hencrypt hwidth.secret_length⟩

end Cslib.Crypto.Homomorphic.FixedKey
